# Proper Feature List for OUR Product — Deduplicated

## A. Website library

- Website profiles — Identify and organize each website as a research entity.
- Domain — Store the website domain.
- Category — Classify the website by category.
- Industry — Classify the website by industry.
- Website type — Classify the website by type.
- Page library — Maintain the pages belonging to each website.
- Site map — Show the website's page/URL structure.
- Website versions — Store multiple captured versions of a website.
- Historical captures — Preserve past website captures for comparison.
- Capture timestamp — Record when each capture was taken.
- Technology stack — Record detected technologies used by the site.
- CMS — Detect and record the content-management system.
- Framework — Detect and record the application framework.
- Libraries — Detect and record notable libraries.
- Hosting/CDN detection — Detect hosting and CDN infrastructure.
- Fonts — Detect fonts used by the website.
- Analytics technology — Detect analytics technologies.
- Payment technology — Detect payment technologies.

## B. Page library

- Page screenshots — Capture individual page screenshots.
- Full-page screenshots — Capture the complete page from top to bottom.
- Above-the-fold screenshot — Capture the initial viewport area.
- Section screenshots — Capture individual page sections for focused research.
- Desktop versions — Store desktop page variants.
- Tablet versions — Store tablet page variants.
- Mobile versions — Store mobile page variants.
- Page metadata — Store structured metadata for each page.
- URL — Store the page URL.
- Title — Store the page title.
- Description — Store the page description.
- H1/H2 structure — Extract heading hierarchy.
- SEO metadata — Extract search-engine metadata.
- OpenGraph metadata — Extract OpenGraph sharing metadata.

